.TH DEEPWORK-DAEMON 8 "" "DeepWork" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
deepwork-daemon \- the DeepWork service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B deepwork-daemon
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Enforces DeepWork's blocks with administrator rights: the hosts file, browser policies, closing
blocked apps, the network protections and locks. It runs as the \fBdeepwork\fR systemd service;
the app and \fBdeepworkctl\fR talk to it over /run/deepwork/deepwork.sock.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-allow\-user " uid"
Let a user control DeepWork (added to /etc/deepwork/config.json), then exit. Restart the service
to apply.
.TP
.B \-\-cleanup
Remove DeepWork's entries from the hosts file, the browser policies and the firewall, and give
administrator rights back after hardcore mode, then exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-sandbox " dir"
Keep all files under \fIdir\fR and don't touch the system (for testing).
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " path"
Listen on \fIpath\fR instead of the default socket.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
/var/lib/deepwork/state.json
Blocks, locks, statistics and settings.
.TP
/etc/deepwork/config.json
Who may control DeepWork (\fBallowed_users\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR deepwork (1),
.BR deepworkctl (1)
